---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/schema.js';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.js';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }];
const updated = SITE.editorial.lastReviewed;
---
<Base title="Privacy"
      description="How PainBeacon handles the information you share, including the optional contact details submitted through our clinic-finder."
      jsonld={breadcrumbLd(crumbs)}>
  <div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Plain-language summary of what we collect, why, and your choices. Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an independent directory that helps people find pain-medicine
      clinics. We are a directory and information service — not a medical provider —
      and nothing here is medical advice.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you use our “Find your pain specialist” tool, we may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The <strong>city or ZIP</strong> you enter and the <strong>type of care</strong> you select.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>name and contact details</strong> — only if you choose “connect me” and enter them. This is optional; you can use the directory without providing them.</li>
      <li>Basic technical information your browser sends automatically (such as device/browser type), used to operate and secure the site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We intentionally do <strong>not</strong> ask for detailed medical history, diagnoses,
      or other sensitive health information through this tool.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To help match you with relevant clinics and improve the directory.</li>
      <li>If — and only if — you choose “connect me,” we may share your contact details
        with a clinic so they can reach out to help you book. If you don’t opt in, we
        don’t share your contact information for that purpose.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell detailed personal health information.</p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We use reputable third-party services to run the site — for example, cloud
      hosting and database providers to store submissions securely, mapping tiles to
      display clinic locations, and public data sources (including the U.S. federal NPI
      registry and public business listing information) to build clinic profiles. These
      providers process data on our behalf under their own terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the locate button on the clinic map, your browser asks your permission
      first, and the answer is used only in your browser to center the map — it is never
      stored and never sent to us.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can browse the entire directory without submitting any information.</li>
      <li>To request access to, correction of, or deletion of contact details you
        submitted, email us at <a href="mailto:privacy@painbeacon.com">privacy@painbeacon.com</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS, and submitted contact details are stored so that
      they are not publicly readable. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly
      secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect your information.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the site evolves; the “last updated” date above
      reflects the current version. Questions? Email
      <a href="mailto:privacy@painbeacon.com">privacy@painbeacon.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
